========================================================================
(B) ADD-9 pt(6) REFUTED: a(n)/n! overshoots e, peaks at n=8, descends to e
========================================================================
  e = 2.718282
  n= 2  a(n)/n!= 1.5000   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  2.0]
  n= 3  a(n)/n!= 2.1667   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  2.5]
  n= 4  a(n)/n!= 2.8750   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  3.0]
  n= 5  a(n)/n!= 3.5083   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  3.5]
  n= 6  a(n)/n!= 3.9819   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  4.0]
  n= 7  a(n)/n!= 4.2613   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  4.5]
  n= 8  a(n)/n!= 4.3594   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  5.0]
  n= 9  a(n)/n!= 4.3190   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  5.5]
  n=10  a(n)/n!= 4.1926   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  6.0]
  n=11  a(n)/n!= 4.0266   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  6.5]
  n=12  a(n)/n!= 3.8544   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  7.0]
  n=13  a(n)/n!= 3.6958   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  7.5]
  n=14  a(n)/n!= 3.5592   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  8.0]
  n=15  a(n)/n!= 3.4464   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  8.5]
  n=16  a(n)/n!= 3.3552   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  9.0]
  n=17  a(n)/n!= 3.2821   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2=  9.5]
  n=18  a(n)/n!= 3.2233   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2= 10.0]
  n=19  a(n)/n!= 3.1757   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2= 10.5]
  n=20  a(n)/n!= 3.1366   [ADD-9 (n+2)/2= 11.0]
  --> ratio PEAKS at n=8 (4.3594); then strictly DECREASES toward e.
  --> ADD-9's '(n+2)/2' fits only the rising side n<=7 and diverges after the peak.

