========================================================================
(E) the bridge polynomial h_m(k): two ends -> {e, 0}
========================================================================
  WILD end  h_m(m)   = A088368(m)/m!  -> e        (Kotesovec)
  TAME end  h_m(-1)  = (2^m-1)/((-1)^m m!) -> 0    (super-exponential)
  m=2: h_m(m)= 1.5000   h_m(-1)=+1.50000
  m=3: h_m(m)= 2.1667   h_m(-1)=-1.16667
  m=4: h_m(m)= 2.8750   h_m(-1)=+0.62500
  m=5: h_m(m)= 3.5083   h_m(-1)=-0.25833
  m=6: h_m(m)= 3.9819   h_m(-1)=+0.08750
  m=7: h_m(m)= 4.2613   h_m(-1)=-0.02520
  m=8: h_m(m)= 4.3594   h_m(-1)=+0.00632
  => h_m interpolates the bridge from 0 (tame/Mersenne) to e (wild/noncrossing-lists).
